{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 6, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: the result is int: searching in u4\nfind tbl: 10 points, computing in u4, costs from gt1030\n  rewrites the model prices lower (each derived, with what it holds under):\n  cost 3   int(0x3ed >> u32(d) & 1)                 the map [1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1][d] of d as a table in one constant (10 entries of 1 bit) (derived; checked on every point)\n      holds where d in [0, 9] (its range)\n      [1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1][d] at d = 0..9 is [1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1] (evaluated at each of the 10)\n      bits [1*i, 1*i + 1) of 0x3ed hold the value at d = i: shifting right by d and masking reads it\n  subgroup forms: the table [1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1] is a closed form of the index (the map [1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1][lane] of lane as a table in one constant (10 entries of 1 bit), holds where lane in [0, 9] (its range)): computed at each lookup's own index, without a register or a shuffle, the function costs 3 (as written 6.875)\n  cost 3   u4(0x3ed >> u32(d) & 1)                  packed table in one constant\n  cost 7   [1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1][d]        lookup table (baseline)\n  [searched every term up to cost 6: 1677721 distinct columns, bank full; 'more' continues]\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 6, "ok": true, "cmd": "find", "ucas": "find tbl", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "find", "points": 10, "sampled": false, "type": "u4", "model": "gt1030", "peephole": [{"cost": 3, "expr": "int(0x3ed >> u32(d) & 1)", "rewrite": "the map [1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1][d] of d as a table in one constant (10 entries of 1 bit)", "holds_where": "d in [0, 9] (its range)", "derivation": "[1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1][d] at d = 0..9 is [1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1] (evaluated at each of the 10)\nbits [1*i, 1*i + 1) of 0x3ed hold the value at d = i: shifting right by d and masking reads it", "check": "exhaustive"}], "implementations": [{"cost": 3, "expr": "u4(0x3ed >> u32(d) & 1)", "why": "packed table in one constant", "verified": true, "exhaustive": true, "proof": "exhaustive"}, {"cost": 7, "expr": "[1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1][d]", "why": "lookup table (baseline)", "verified": true, "exhaustive": true, "proof": "exhaustive"}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "info", "text": "the result is int: searching in u4"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  note: the result is int: searching in u4\nfind tbl: 10 points, computing in u4, costs from gt1030\n  rewrites the model prices lower (each derived, with what it holds under):\n  cost 3   int(0x3ed >> u32(d) & 1)                 the map [1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1][d] of d as a table in one constant (10 entries of 1 bit) (derived; checked on every point)\n      holds where d in [0, 9] (its range)\n      [1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1][d] at d = 0..9 is [1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1] (evaluated at each of the 10)\n      bits [1*i, 1*i + 1) of 0x3ed hold the value at d = i: shifting right by d and masking reads it\n  subgroup forms: the table [1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1] is a closed form of the index (the map [1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1][lane] of lane as a table in one constant (10 entries of 1 bit), holds where lane in [0, 9] (its range)): computed at each lookup's own index, without a register or a shuffle, the function costs 3 (as written 6.875)\n  cost 3   u4(0x3ed >> u32(d) & 1)                  packed table in one constant\n  cost 7   [1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1][d]        lookup table (baseline)\n  [searched every term up to cost 6: 1677721 distinct columns, bank full; 'more' continues]\n"}, "isError": false}}
